<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="BerniesTune-Dm-Theme" spTempo="180">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1952
Composer:	Bernie Miller
Lyricist:	Jerry Leiber and Mike Stoller
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Cool jazz / bebop
Key:	C minor

“Bernie’s Tune” was composed by Bernie Miller
and became widely known through Gerry Mulligan’s
1952 recording with the Mulligan Quartet. It is an
instrumental contrafact-like jazz tune whose
melody and harmonic movement made it popular
with bebop and cool-jazz musicians; C minor is the
commonly cited key, although arrangements and
transcriptions vary.</spComments>
